WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.790
The Shinobi crouched low on the pagoda roof
and listened to the night air.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:10.250
Up here in the mountains, away from the hustle
and bustle of the markets in town, it was

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.000
almost silent.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.300
Just the distant rattle of shutters somewhere
behind him.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.090
The mountain shrine was tucked out of sight,
so far into the countryside that no one would

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.340
stumble onto it by accident.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.010
No one would come here without a reason.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:30.570
The Shinobi knew the face of his target, a
warlord turned politician, with more blood

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.670
on his hands than the assassin sent to kill
him.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.140
By the burning glow of the night sky, the
Shinobi could see the man kneeling at the

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.140
shrine.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.170
The path was made up of small stones, so he’d
have to drop onto the grass and creep around

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.770
the pond to approach his target.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.899
No guards, no one else was there at all.

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:55.579
This was the spot where the man came to pray
when he was struggling to sleep, perhaps trying

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:58.870
to atone for the lives he’d taken.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.559
Perhaps he didn’t care at all.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:05.560
The ninja drew the blade in total silence
and timed his drop to the ground with the

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.740
rattling noise in the distance.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:13.790
With each dainty step, he closed the distance
to his target, readying the blade over his

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:14.790
head.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.009
It was done in a moment.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.540
The man was dead before his body hit the ground.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.080
He likely didn’t even notice as the steel
had severed the nerves running down his spinal

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.080
cord.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.740
So shard was the blade that it slid through
his bones like a fish through water.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.060
Raising the blade to his eyes, the Shinobi
cleaned it quickly.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.119
If he was seen with blood on his sword, he
would immediately be implicated, not that

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:38.619
he was ever seen.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:43.280
But precautions like this were what kept him
out of sight for all of these years.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.240
When you lived in the Valley of Ashes, the
burial grounds for countless wars, you had

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.140
to become a shadow, become one of the ancient
spirits haunting the woods.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.799
But as he wiped the red from the steel, he
caught a flash of light in the reflection.

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:03.100
An orange glow marking a jagged line across
the metal.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.840
That’s strange, sunset was several hours
ago.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.391
Come to think of it, why was there an orange
glow in the sky?

00:02:10.391 --> 00:02:14.550
He snapped his neck around to see the fires
through the gates into the pagoda’s garden.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:18.739
Down by the ocean’s edge, at the foot of
the mountains, was the city where he has always

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:19.739
lived.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.830
And it was on fire.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:27.470
Leaping up onto the walls, he stood up straight,
surveying the horror scene taking place before

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.470
him.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.250
Thick plumes of smoke billowed up into the
night sky, so dense and large that it seemed

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.470
to become the blackness of the night.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.879
It was hard to make out much of what was going
on down there.

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:43.630
The Shinobi looked everywhere to try to see
the invading army or the rioters, but there

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.810
were none.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.980
Just people running in all directions like
ants out of a flooding nest.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:55.769
But there, moving in amongst the smoke, were
other shapes, impossibly tall, lumbering around

00:02:55.769 --> 00:02:56.769
like… people.

00:02:56.769 --> 00:03:01.890
People that towered over the houses, that
had to crane down to the ground to scoop up

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.160
the poor civilians who were running this way
and that.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.940
The Shinobi stood there, terrified, as he
realized the rattling sound he’d been hearing

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.159
all night wasn’t from any shutters at all.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:17.799
He could do nothing but watch as the trees
in front of him trembled and buckled in all

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:22.440
directions, as a hulking shadowy figure lumbered
towards him.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.440
*

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:29.020
The Imperial Japanese Anomalous Matters Examination
Agency, or the IJAMEA, was a Japanese agency

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:35.000
responsible for tracking a number of mysterious
and often dangerous artifacts, creatures and

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.090
anomalies, prior to the Second World War.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.240
In 1945, the IJAMEA was shut down and absorbed
into the SCP Foundation.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:48.599
All of these data, historic records, and anomalies,
were all transferred over into the Foundation’s

00:03:48.599 --> 00:03:49.599
control.

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:54.579
Reasons for this were partially political
and partially in the interest of world peace.

00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:59.500
The formation of the IJAMEA was influenced
heavily by Japan’s ties with Germany in

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.830
the first half of the 20th century.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:06.989
The Imperial German Anomalous Matters Examination
Agency was the blueprint for their Japanese

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:07.989
equivalent.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:13.079
However, with increasing militarism in Japan
throughout the 20th century, the IJAMEA became

00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:17.930
increasingly obsessed with trying to harness
their anomalous discoveries in the interests

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.720
of military power.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.840
Their goal became the establishment of a Yokai
Battalion, powerful enough to establish them

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.310
as one of, if not the world’s greatest superpower.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:33.530
Following the bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki,
Japan surrendered in the Second World War

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.100
and agreed to dissolve its military, including
the IJAMEA.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.540
That left the Foundation with the task of
picking up the threads left behind and trying

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.860
to come up with new ways of securing, containing,
and protecting some of Japan’s most deadly

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.080
SCPs.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:55.870
Few more deadly and evasive than the entities
that were too much even for the Yokai Battalion.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.280
SCP-2863.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.280
*

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:03.970
In 1946, clean-up operations were in full
effect, trying to deal with the fallout from

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.400
the atomic bomb dropped on Nagasaki.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.180
Crews dressed in led-lined suits worked around
the clock burying radioactive material and

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.840
trying to remove as much contaminated debris
as possible.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.690
Rebuilding the city was still a long way off.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:23.690
At various points, the wind would kick up
and carry the dust left behind into the air,

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.400
creating a dangerous radioactive haze.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.100
Crews continued to work through such conditions
as the understanding of airborne contamination

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.430
was still in its infancy.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.220
Watanabe Goro was one such worker.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.550
Midway through a night shift and clasping
a damp rag to his mouth, he pushed on through

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:43.340
the dust, clearing out building after building.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:47.390
They had spent the morning carrying corpses
out of an unidentifiable building.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.550
The corpses themselves were pretty much worn
away too.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.630
Just skeletons, really, charred by the blast
from months before.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:59.740
As Goro staggered along the street, he kept
feeling like he was imagining things.

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:03.850
The long hours and traumatic conditions were
enough to make him see all kinds of things

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:09.400
in his dreams, but he kept feeling like his
dreams were starting to creep into the real

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.400
world.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.240
Shadows kept moving through the haze all around
him, taller than buildings, staggering around

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.690
as if they were drunk.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:21.340
They had been appearing all night, just out
of sight, but always close by.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:24.360
He stopped and leaned against what was left
of a brick wall.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.919
There was one of his hallucinations now, just
up ahead of him.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:32.229
The husks of buildings on either side of him
were about as tall as their knees.

00:06:32.229 --> 00:06:35.009
It must have been thirty meters tall, at least.

00:06:35.009 --> 00:06:40.180
But its legs were strange, there seemed to
be a gap in the middle of each of them.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.380
They were skinny, no… skeletal.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.400
The skeleton’s foot crushed a car right
in front of him.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.750
The crunch of metal was loud enough to snap
Goro out of his stupor.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.720
This wasn’t a hallucination.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.500
Hallucinations can’t crush cars.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:58.440
With a yelp, he tumbled backwards, staring
up into the haze of dust.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:03.800
He saw the shadow of a pelvis, above it what
must have been a ribcage the size of his house,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.150
but the creature disappeared into the darkness
and the dust.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:12.910
If it was too tall for him to see its face,
maybe it was too tall to see him on the ground

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.910
as well.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.810
The skeleton stopped, standing directly over
him.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.840
For a second, he thought that maybe he’d
be okay.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:25.419
But then, with a great rattling rumble, the
monster hunched down low, and the enormous

00:07:25.419 --> 00:07:29.460
skull appeared out of the haze, flying right
toward him.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:33.740
He managed to dodge its gnashing teeth, but
it caught his foot, sending him rolling through

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.229
the radioactive dirt.

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:39.750
Goro didn’t give himself a moment to recover,
though, he took off running as fast as he

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:44.000
could, hearing the rattling sound terrifyingly
close behind his back.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.000
*

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.190
You will be pleased to know that Watanabe
Goro survived this incident.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:52.699
With only minor injuries, he managed to navigate
his way to the nearest police station, where

00:07:52.699 --> 00:07:58.389
SCP agents, already familiar with the entity
he had encountered, took control of the situation.

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:02.759
The so-called Starving Skeletons had been
roaming the bomb sites for several weeks by

00:08:02.759 --> 00:08:03.780
that point.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:08.389
It was the Foundation’s first exposure to
one of the oldest known entities that the

00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:11.980
IJAMEA had been studying for years.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:17.900
To date, 206 separate instances of SCP-2863
have been officially recorded.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:23.520
However, the myth of the Gashadokuro has been
circulating in various parts of Japan since

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.440
the tenth century at least.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.740
Giant skeletons were said to haunt the sites
of particularly deadly battles, hunting by

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.610
night and feeding on the blood of their human
victims.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:39.300
These myths tally up with what the Foundation
currently knows about these entities.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:45.430
Instances of SCP-2863 only appear after sunset
and will lose all corporeality when exposed

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:50.050
to sunlight in the morning or any light source
over 1.1 lux.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:55.560
To give you some reference for that, moonlight
typically falls between 0.25 and 1 lux.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:01.029
A typical room with the light on will be one
hundred or even one thousand times brighter.

00:09:01.029 --> 00:09:05.990
As you can imagine, this has made them virtually
impossible to contain as they manifest and

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.800
unmanifest outside of controllable conditions.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:13.920
They seem to have continuous existence in
some way however, as previously neutralized

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.410
instances can and will reappear later on.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:22.560
In folklore, the Gashadokuro are spirits that
take control of skeletons.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:27.350
Some hesitant researchers have posited that
perhaps the instances that dematerialize are

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.770
returning to their spirit form.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.340
Little is understood about what that means
in practice.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:36.490
What is more, this SCP cannot be photographed.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:42.190
All attempts to capture them on film or digital
cameras have failed, including video tests.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:46.760
It is theorized that there is a link between
them not appearing on camera and their disappearance

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.270
when exposed to light.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:52.070
Again, quite what link could be is still mostly
unknown.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:57.570
Due to a steady increase in urban development
in Japan and ongoing peace in the region,

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.709
appearances of this SCP are growing increasingly
rare.

00:10:00.709 --> 00:10:05.490
While this marks a positive change for the
people of Japan, it makes it even more difficult

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.940
to study this SCP and learn how to prevent
it in the future.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:15.441
The most recent fatality to occur at the bony
hands of SCP-2863 happened in 2008, and it

00:10:15.441 --> 00:10:17.750
was as part of a Foundation experiment.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:23.110
While most of Hiroshima and Nagasaki have
been redeveloped into bustling metropolitan

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:29.060
areas, the outskirts of each city, particularly
several parks, saw occasional instances of

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.150
SCP-2863 appearing at night.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:37.870
As such, the SCP Foundation conducted a series
of experiments under cover of nightfall, releasing

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:43.579
D-class personnel into a park in Hiroshima
to observe how the SCPs hunted humans.

00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:49.220
Their enormous height, towering at over 30m,
gave them a huge advantage, being able to

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.019
chase people down with little difficulty.

00:10:52.019 --> 00:10:55.120
Another notable thing about them is just how
quietly they move.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:59.830
There is a gentle rattling sound that follows
them around, but aside from that, they are

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:05.269
very light-footed and difficult to detect
until they are right on top of you.

00:11:05.269 --> 00:11:08.410
This isn’t helped by the fact that they
hunt at night.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.000
As a result, they are remarkably quick at
catching their prey.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.910
Once they have snatched their victims up in
their skeletal fingers, they perform the same

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:17.590
eating ritual every time.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:20.500
They eat the person and consume their blood.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:26.130
Initially confused by this finding, the Foundation
was unsure where the blood was going as the

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:29.110
skeletons had no obvious digestive system.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:33.100
After the release of several more D-class
personnel into the park, they still weren’t

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:38.100
certain but believed that the SCP instances
were absorbing the blood into their bones

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.370
in some way.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:43.709
Further testing was requested but denied due
to the sheer number of D-class fatalities

00:11:43.709 --> 00:11:44.850
in the area.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:49.290
They were starting to run out, and would have
to ship more of them across to Japan, which

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:52.620
was just a bit inconvenient for everyone involved.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:58.310
As the outskirts of those cities have been
urbanized, the instances of SCP-2863 have

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:03.000
reduced to the point that a smaller contingent
of agents and researchers are now left in

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.000
place.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.870
The light pollution from these areas is enough
to prevent them from being able to manifest

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:10.100
in the first place for the most part.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:15.570
Only on the rare occasion of power outages
have Mobile Task Force 03 been deployed.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:20.210
Whilst researching this SCP, the Foundation
came across an account from a Shinobi in the

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.210
1700s.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:26.050
It was rare to find any kind of written document
from a ninja for obvious reasons, but the

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:30.680
account discovered painted a harrowing picture
of just how much damage these Yokai could

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.560
inflict upon a city.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:38.180
The nameless Shinobi first encountered SCP-2863
while assassinating an unnamed target in the

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.440
mountains above his fishing town.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:45.850
Looking down on the fires below him, he saw
human shapes walking through the smoke, dwarfing

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:50.560
the buildings they moved between, before an
instance charged through the trees straight

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:51.560
at him.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:55.279
Diving out of the way, the Shinobi quickly
melted into the shadows.

00:12:55.279 --> 00:12:58.410
Both man and demon hunted one another through
the night.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:02.660
He managed to climb onto its spine and inflict
what he was certain would be a killing blow

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:07.480
to the skeleton, only for his blade to bounce
right off the bone.

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:11.500
Caught and vulnerable for the first time in
his life, the Shinobi was helpless as the

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:15.459
spirit threw him from its back into the courtyard
and charged at him.

00:13:15.459 --> 00:13:20.750
It was only the hem of the ninja’s sleeve
catching fire from a candle that saved him.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:25.990
Just as the skeleton was about to bite down
on his head, the light flared, and the SCP

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.310
disappeared entirely.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:31.210
For a long while, the man lay in the courtyard,
pondering his actions.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:34.480
He should have died that night, yet he survived.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:38.690
Getting slowly to his feet, the man knew now
what his destiny was.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:42.540
A monster that strikes from the shadows, scared
of the light.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:46.029
He and the Gashadokuro were not so different.

00:13:46.029 --> 00:13:49.720
Understanding his target was the step to defeating
them.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.750
Snatching up a lantern from the ground, the
Shinobi descended the mountain into the wreckage

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:56.400
of his hometown and defended his people.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:01.080
By night, he would emerge hunting down the
Gashadokuro under the cover of darkness, banishing

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.899
them with the light hidden under a dark sheet.

00:14:03.899 --> 00:14:08.020
The man fought night after night, narrowly
risking death, to save his people from the

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.080
onslaught of the evil spirit.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:14.940
A small plaque was installed by the IJAMEA
shortly before the Foundation took over the

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.320
management of the SCP.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:21.920
It was installed at the foot of an old pagoda
just outside a small fishing village.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.399
On it was a simple haiku.

00:14:24.399 --> 00:14:27.610
Walking in shadow,
In the midst of our demons,

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.720
We will find the light.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:34.929
Now check out “SCP-2662 - Cthulhu” and
“SCP–2935 – O, Death!”

